  "backlogcachecap": {
    "title": "backlogCacheCap",
    "desc": "Capacity of the **L3 Backlog Cache** unverified staging buffer (ADR-028).\n\n### How It Works\n- Pre-picks candidate coordinates along the spiral without performing any chunk loads or database writes.\n- Each region pulse picks the oldest candidate, determines its 32x32 Anvil/Linear region file bin, and classifies all candidates in that bin off-tick in one amortized pass.\n- Keeps the verified `cacheCap` constantly replenished so `/rtp` teleports are instantaneous.\n- On `rtp-lite`, defaults to `0` (disabled) to conserve RAM.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Capacity of the <b>L3 Backlog Cache<\/b> unverified staging buffer (ADR-028).<\/p>\n<h4 style=\"margin:12px 0 6px; color:var(--green); font-size:0.9rem;\">How It Works<\/h4>\n<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 6px 18px; padding:0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Pre-picks candidate coordinates along the spiral without performing any chunk loads or database writes.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Each region pulse picks the oldest candidate, determines its 32x32 Anvil/Linear region file bin, and classifies all candidates in that bin off-tick in one amortized pass.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Keeps the verified <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>cacheCap<\/b><\/code> constantly replenished so <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>/rtp<\/b><\/code> teleports are instantaneous.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">On <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>rtp-lite<\/b><\/code>, defaults to <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>0<\/b><\/code> (disabled) to conserve RAM.<\/li>\n<\/ul>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer | Default: 1000 (lite: 0) | Docs: REGIONS.md (ADR-028)",
    "defaultVal": "1000",
    "defaultSnippet": "backlogCacheCap: 1000"
  },
  "activechunkcap": {
    "title": "activeChunkCap",
    "desc": "Maximum number of chunks held in the **L1 Hot Queue** with loaded chunk tickets (`keep(true)`) for zero-latency instant teleports.\n\n- When a location is verified, its chunk is kept loaded in L1.\n- If L1 reaches `activeChunkCap`, additional verified locations are demoted to the L2 Cold Queue (chunks released from memory, reloaded asynchronously on demand).\n- Prevents server RAM exhaustion and force-loading leaks (S-002).",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Maximum number of chunks held in the <b>L1 Hot Queue<\/b> with loaded chunk tickets (<code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>keep(true)<\/b><\/code>) for zero-latency instant teleports.<\/p>\n<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 6px 18px; padding:0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">When a location is verified, its chunk is kept loaded in L1.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">If L1 reaches <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>activeChunkCap<\/b><\/code>, additional verified locations are demoted to the L2 Cold Queue (chunks released from memory, reloaded asynchronously on demand).<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Prevents server RAM exhaustion and force-loading leaks (S-002).<\/li>\n<\/ul>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer | Default: 10 | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "10",
    "defaultSnippet": "activeChunkCap: 10"
  },
  "price": {
    "title": "price",
    "desc": "Vault economy cost deducted from the player upon successful teleportation.\n\n- Set to `0.0` for free teleports.\n- If teleportation fails or is cancelled, fees are refunded automatically according to `economy.yml`.\n- Accepts `@economy` to inherit global economy defaults.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Vault economy cost deducted from the player upon successful teleportation.<\/p>\n<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 6px 18px; padding:0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Set to <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>0.0<\/b><\/code> for free teleports.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">If teleportation fails or is cancelled, fees are refunded automatically according to <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>economy.yml<\/b><\/code>.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Accepts <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>@economy<\/b><\/code> to inherit global economy defaults.<\/li>\n<\/ul>",
    "meta": "Type: Double >= 0.0 | Unit: Currency | Docs: ECONOMY.md",
    "defaultVal": "0.0",
    "defaultSnippet": "price: 0.0"
  },
  "spatialresolution": {
    "title": "spatialResolution",
    "desc": "Spatial resolution for MemoryShape rejection tracking (positive integer or 'auto').",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Spatial resolution for MemoryShape rejection tracking (positive integer or 'auto').<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer >= 1 or 'auto' | Default: auto | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "\"auto\"",
    "defaultSnippet": "spatialResolution: \"auto\""
  },
  "version": {
    "title": "version",
    "desc": "Internal config version. **Do not modify.**",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Internal config version. <b>Do not modify.<\/b><\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: String | Default: `\"1.1\"` | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "`\"1.1\"`",
    "defaultSnippet": "version: `\"1.1\"`"
  },
  "shapename": {
    "title": "shape.name",
    "desc": "Shape engine: `CIRCLE`, `CIRCLE_NORMAL`, `CIRCLE_OPTIMIZED_DUAL_LAYER`, `CIRCLE_DEPRECATED_PURE_SPIRAL`, `SQUARE`, `SQUARE_NORMAL`, `SQUARE_OPTIMIZED_DUAL_LAYER`, `SQUARE_DEPRECATED_PURE_SPIRAL`, `ELLIPSE`, `RECTANGLE`, `POLYGON`.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Shape engine: <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>CIRCLE<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>CIRCLE_NORMAL<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>CIRCLE_OPTIMIZED_DUAL_LAYER<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>CIRCLE_DEPRECATED_PURE_SPIRAL<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>SQUARE<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>SQUARE_NORMAL<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>SQUARE_OPTIMIZED_DUAL_LAYER<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>SQUARE_DEPRECATED_PURE_SPIRAL<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>ELLIPSE<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>RECTANGLE<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>POLYGON<\/b><\/code>.<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: String | Docs: CONFIGURATION.md",
    "defaultVal": "",
    "defaultSnippet": ""
  },
  "name": {
    "title": "name",
    "desc": "Vertical adjustor engine: `JUMP`, `LINEAR`, or `FIXED`.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Vertical adjustor engine: <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>JUMP<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>LINEAR<\/b><\/code>, or <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>FIXED<\/b><\/code>.<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: String | Default: `\"JUMP\"` | Docs: CONFIGURATION.md",
    "defaultVal": "`\"JUMP\"`",
    "defaultSnippet": "name: `\"JUMP\"`"
  },
  "shapemode": {
    "title": "shape.mode",
    "desc": "Selection logic. See table below.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Selection logic. See table below.<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: String | Docs: CONFIGURATION.md",
    "defaultVal": "",
    "defaultSnippet": ""
  },
  "mode": {
    "title": "mode",
    "desc": "Coordinate candidate selection algorithm within the region boundary.\n\n- **`ACCUMULATE`**: *(Recommended)* Pre-computes sector weights along a 1D Archimedean spiral mapping (ADR-001) or continuous Hilbert space (ADR-085). Produces uniform dispersion without clustering.\n- **`NEAREST`**: Picks the nearest safe coordinate. Fast, but repeatedly places players in similar areas.\n- **`REROLL`**: Random uniform sampling with retries.\n- **`NONE`**: Pure spiral walk with zero pre-computation. Essential for massive radii (> 50,000 blocks / 3,125 chunks) to avoid long startup calculation.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Coordinate candidate selection algorithm within the region boundary.<\/p>\n<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 6px 18px; padding:0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>ACCUMULATE<\/b><\/code><\/b>: <i>(Recommended)<\/i> Pre-computes sector weights along a 1D Archimedean spiral mapping (ADR-001) or continuous Hilbert space (ADR-085). Produces uniform dispersion without clustering.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>NEAREST<\/b><\/code><\/b>: Picks the nearest safe coordinate. Fast, but repeatedly places players in similar areas.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>REROLL<\/b><\/code><\/b>: Random uniform sampling with retries.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>NONE<\/b><\/code><\/b>: Pure spiral walk with zero pre-computation. Essential for massive radii (> 50,000 blocks / 3,125 chunks) to avoid long startup calculation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>",
    "meta": "Type: Enum [ACCUMULATE, NEAREST, REROLL, NONE] | Default: ACCUMULATE | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "ACCUMULATE",
    "defaultSnippet": "mode: \"ACCUMULATE\""
  },
  "shapecenterx": {
    "title": "shape.centerX",
    "desc": "Center of the region in chunks (or with explicit unit suffixes).",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Center of the region in chunks (or with explicit unit suffixes).<\/p>",
    "meta": "Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "",
    "defaultSnippet": ""
  },
  "centerx": {
    "title": "centerX",
    "desc": "Horizontal X coordinate of region center (in chunk coordinates). Multiply by 16 for block coordinate.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Horizontal X coordinate of region center (in chunk coordinates). Multiply by 16 for block coordinate.<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer | Default: 0 | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "0",
    "defaultSnippet": "centerX: 0"
  },
  "shapecenterz": {
    "title": "shape.centerZ",
    "desc": "Center of the region in chunks (or with explicit unit suffixes).",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Center of the region in chunks (or with explicit unit suffixes).<\/p>",
    "meta": "Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "",
    "defaultSnippet": ""
  },
  "centerz": {
    "title": "centerZ",
    "desc": "Horizontal Z coordinate of region center (in chunk coordinates). Multiply by 16 for block coordinate.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Horizontal Z coordinate of region center (in chunk coordinates). Multiply by 16 for block coordinate.<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer | Default: 0 | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "0",
    "defaultSnippet": "centerZ: 0"
  },
  "shapeuniqueplacements": {
    "title": "shape.uniquePlacements",
    "desc": "Chunk radius cleared around each used location so it is never reused. `0` = off (default), `1` = the landing chunk only, `N` = an `(2N-1)x(2N-1)` chunk square centred on the landing chunk. (Legacy `true`/`false` are still accepted and map to `1`/`0`.)",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Chunk radius cleared around each used location so it is never reused. <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>0<\/b><\/code> = off (default), <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>1<\/b><\/code> = the landing chunk only, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>N<\/b><\/code> = an <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>(2N-1)x(2N-1)<\/b><\/code> chunk square centred on the landing chunk. (Legacy <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>true<\/b><\/code>/<code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>false<\/b><\/code> are still accepted and map to <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>1<\/b><\/code>/<code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>0<\/b><\/code>.)<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer | Docs: CONFIGURATION.md",
    "defaultVal": "",
    "defaultSnippet": ""
  },
  "uniqueplacements": {
    "title": "uniquePlacements",
    "desc": "Chunk radius cleared around a landing spot once consumed so it is never reused for future teleports.\n\n- **`0`**: Off (spots can be reused).\n- **`1`**: The landing chunk only is retired.\n- **`N`**: An `(2N-1)x(2N-1)` chunk square around the landing is retired.\n- **`auto`**: Automatically matches the server's effective view distance (lowest power of 2 at or under view distance, e.g. 10 -> 8 chunks).\n\nWhen paired with `expand: true` in dual-layer shapes, it enables zero-memory dyadic stride downsampling ($S = (2R_u-1)^2$), keeping concurrent players isolated by view distance while driving outward frontier expansion.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Chunk radius cleared around a landing spot once consumed so it is never reused for future teleports.<\/p>\n<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 6px 18px; padding:0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>0<\/b><\/code><\/b>: Off (spots can be reused).<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>1<\/b><\/code><\/b>: The landing chunk only is retired.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>N<\/b><\/code><\/b>: An <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>(2N-1)x(2N-1)<\/b><\/code> chunk square around the landing is retired.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>auto<\/b><\/code><\/b>: Automatically matches the server's effective view distance (lowest power of 2 at or under view distance, e.g. 10 -> 8 chunks).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">When paired with <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>expand: true<\/b><\/code> in dual-layer shapes, it enables zero-memory dyadic stride downsampling ($S = (2R_u-1)^2$), keeping concurrent players isolated by view distance while driving outward frontier expansion.<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer / 'auto' | Default: 0 | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "\"auto\"",
    "defaultSnippet": "uniquePlacements: \"auto\""
  },
  "shaperadius": {
    "title": "shape.radius",
    "desc": "**Outer** bound. Players never land farther than this from the center. Supports suffixes (e.g. `4096b`, `256c`, `4r`, `5km`).",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\"><b>Outer<\/b> bound. Players never land farther than this from the center. Supports suffixes (e.g. <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>4096b<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>256c<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>4r<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>5km<\/b><\/code>).<\/p>",
    "meta": "Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "",
    "defaultSnippet": ""
  },
  "radius": {
    "title": "radius",
    "desc": "**Outer coordinate limit** of the region. Players will never land farther than this distance from the center.\n\n### Unit Interpretation\n- By default, plain numbers without a suffix are measured in **chunks** (`1 chunk = 16 blocks`).\n- Supports explicit suffixes:\n  - `256c` / `256chunks` = 4,096 blocks\n  - `4096b` / `4096blocks` = 4,096 blocks\n  - `4r` / `4regions` = 2,048 blocks (1 region = 32 chunks)\n  - `5km` = 5,000 blocks\n  - `3mi` = 4,828 blocks\n  - `500nb` = 4,000 Overworld blocks (Nether coordinates)\n\n> \ud83d\udca1 **Inheritance:** In `regions/<name>.yml`, `shape: \"@config\"` inherits `defaults.shape.radius` from `config.yml`.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\"><b>Outer coordinate limit<\/b> of the region. Players will never land farther than this distance from the center.<\/p>\n<h4 style=\"margin:12px 0 6px; color:var(--green); font-size:0.9rem;\">Unit Interpretation<\/h4>\n<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 6px 18px; padding:0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">By default, plain numbers without a suffix are measured in <b>chunks<\/b> (<code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>1 chunk = 16 blocks<\/b><\/code>).<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Supports explicit suffixes:<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>256c<\/b><\/code> / <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>256chunks<\/b><\/code> = 4,096 blocks<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>4096b<\/b><\/code> / <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>4096blocks<\/b><\/code> = 4,096 blocks<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>4r<\/b><\/code> / <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>4regions<\/b><\/code> = 2,048 blocks (1 region = 32 chunks)<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>5km<\/b><\/code> = 5,000 blocks<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>3mi<\/b><\/code> = 4,828 blocks<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>500nb<\/b><\/code> = 4,000 Overworld blocks (Nether coordinates)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--accent); padding:4px 8px; margin:6px 0; background:rgba(137, 180, 250, 0.08); font-size:0.8rem; color:var(--subtext);\">\ud83d\udca1 <b>Inheritance:<\/b> In <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>regions/<name>.yml<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>shape: \"@config\"<\/b><\/code> inherits <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>defaults.shape.radius<\/b><\/code> from <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>config.yml<\/b><\/code>.<\/div>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer / Distance Suffix | Default: 256c (4,096 blocks) | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "4096b",
    "defaultSnippet": "radius: 4096b"
  },
  "shapecenterradius": {
    "title": "shape.centerRadius",
    "desc": "**Inner** bound (donut hole). Players never land closer than this to the center. Supports suffixes (e.g. `1000b`, `64c`).",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\"><b>Inner<\/b> bound (donut hole). Players never land closer than this to the center. Supports suffixes (e.g. <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>1000b<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>64c<\/b><\/code>).<\/p>",
    "meta": "Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "",
    "defaultSnippet": ""
  },
  "centerradius": {
    "title": "centerRadius",
    "desc": "**Inner exclusion deadzone** radius (the \"donut hole\"). Players will never land closer than this distance to the center.\n\n### Key Rules\n- Protects spawn monuments, lobbies, central claims, and populated hubs from teleport traffic.\n- **Must be strictly smaller than `radius`**. If `centerRadius >= radius`, the selectable band is empty.\n- Total pickable band width is `radius - centerRadius` chunks.\n- Supports spatial suffixes (e.g. `64c`, `1000b`, `1r`).",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\"><b>Inner exclusion deadzone<\/b> radius (the \"donut hole\"). Players will never land closer than this distance to the center.<\/p>\n<h4 style=\"margin:12px 0 6px; color:var(--green); font-size:0.9rem;\">Key Rules<\/h4>\n<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 6px 18px; padding:0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Protects spawn monuments, lobbies, central claims, and populated hubs from teleport traffic.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\"><b>Must be strictly smaller than <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>radius<\/b><\/code><\/b>. If <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>centerRadius >= radius<\/b><\/code>, the selectable band is empty.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Total pickable band width is <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>radius - centerRadius<\/b><\/code> chunks.<\/li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Supports spatial suffixes (e.g. <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>64c<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>1000b<\/b><\/code>, <code style=\\\"color:var(--yellow);\\\"><b>1r<\/b><\/code>).<\/li>\n<\/ul>",
    "meta": "Type: Integer / Distance Suffix | Default: 64c (1,024 blocks) | Docs: REGIONS.md",
    "defaultVal": "64",
    "defaultSnippet": "centerRadius: 64"
  },
  "shapeweight": {
    "title": "shape.weight",
    "desc": "Distribution weight across the vertex bounding box.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:6px 0; font-size:0.82rem; line-height:1.4;\">Distribution weight across the vertex bounding box.<\/p>",
    "meta": "Type: Double | Default: `1.0` | Docs: CONFIGURATION.md",
    "defaultVal": "`1.0`",
    "defaultSnippet": "weight: `1.0`"
